/** @page sshauthguide Authentication Guide

    @tableofcontents

    @section sshauthflow Authentication Flow Overview

    Every SSH authentication attempt passes through a well-defined pipeline:

    -# The listener's @ref Qore::Ssh::SshListenerConfig "SshListenerConfig.enabled_auth_methods"
       list filters which methods the session will accept.  Disabled methods are
       rejected at the transport layer and never reach the auth provider.
    -# If @ref Qore::Ssh::SshListenerConfig "SshListenerConfig.auth_banner" is
       set, the server sends the banner text to the client before the first auth
       exchange.
    -# @ref Qore::Ssh::SshServer::authenticateSession() "SshServer::authenticateSession()"
       waits for the client's auth request, builds a
       @ref Qore::Ssh::SshAuthContextInfo "SshAuthContextInfo", and calls the
       configured @c auth_provider or @c auth_callback.
    -# The provider returns a @ref Qore::Ssh::SshAuthDecision "SshAuthDecision".
       When @c accepted is @c True and @c partial is @c False the session is
       fully authenticated and the decision's @c command_policy, @c sftp_policy,
       and @c session_data are attached to the session.
    -# When @c partial is @c True the server loops back to step 3, allowing the
       client to satisfy additional auth methods (multi-factor).

    @section sshauthmethods Supported Authentication Methods

    The module recognises six method names that correspond to standard SSH
    authentication types:

    | Method        | Description                                    |
    |---------------|------------------------------------------------|
    | @c none       | No credentials required                        |
    | @c password   | Username and password                          |
    | @c publickey  | Public-key signature verification              |
    | @c interactive| Keyboard-interactive challenge-response        |
    | @c hostbased  | Host-based authentication                      |
    | @c gssapi-mic | GSSAPI with MIC (Kerberos)                     |

    Only methods listed in
    @ref Qore::Ssh::SshListenerConfig "SshListenerConfig.enabled_auth_methods"
    are offered to clients.  When the field is unset the default set is
    @c none, @c password, @c publickey, and @c interactive.

    @section sshauthconfigdriven Config-Driven Authentication with VirtualSshAuthProvider

    @ref SshServerAuthProvider::VirtualSshAuthProvider "VirtualSshAuthProvider"
    provides a declarative, config-driven auth provider.  Configure it through
    @c VirtualSshAuthProviderOptions
    and attach it to the server via
    @ref Qore::Ssh::SshServerConfig "SshServerConfig.auth_provider".

    @subsection sshauthpassword Password Authentication Example

    @code{.py}
VirtualSshAuthProvider provider(<VirtualSshAuthProviderOptions>{
    "methods": ("password",),
    "password": <VirtualSshPasswordAuthOptions>{
        "users": (
            <VirtualSshPasswordUserInfo>{
                "username": "alice",
                "password": "secret",
                "decision": <VirtualSshAuthDecisionTemplate>{
                    "principal": "principal:alice",
                },
            },
        ),
    },
});
    @endcode

    Each method section supports @c allowed_usernames / @c denied_usernames
    filtering and an optional @c validator callback for app-level logic.

    @subsection sshauthpubkey Public-Key Authentication Example

    @code{.py}
VirtualSshAuthProvider provider(<VirtualSshAuthProviderOptions>{
    "methods": ("publickey",),
    "publickey": <VirtualSshPublicKeyAuthOptions>{
        "authorized_keys": (
            <VirtualSshAuthorizedKeyInfo>{
                "username": "bob",
                "public_key": key_data,
                "public_key_type": "ssh-ed25519",
            },
        ),
    },
});
    @endcode

    @section sshauthmfa Multi-Factor Authentication

    Set @ref SshServerAuthProvider::VirtualSshAuthProviderOptions "VirtualSshAuthProviderOptions.required_methods"
    to an ordered list of methods that must all succeed.  After each
    individual method succeeds, @ref SshServerAuthProvider::VirtualSshAuthProvider "VirtualSshAuthProvider"
    checks whether all required methods have been completed:

    - If methods remain, the decision is returned with @c partial = @c True,
      @c allowed_auth_methods listing the remaining methods, and the
      @c session_data key @c "__completed_auth_methods" tracking progress.
    - When the final method succeeds, @c partial is cleared and the session
      is fully authenticated.

    The server's @c authenticateSession() loop drives the partial-auth
    handshake automatically -- each partial decision causes it to wait for
    the next client auth request.

    @code{.py}
VirtualSshAuthProvider provider(<VirtualSshAuthProviderOptions>{
    "methods": ("none", "password"),
    "required_methods": ("none", "password"),
    "none": <VirtualSshStaticAuthMethodOptions>{
        "allowed_usernames": ("alice",),
    },
    "password": <VirtualSshPasswordAuthOptions>{
        "users": (
            <VirtualSshPasswordUserInfo>{
                "username": "alice",
                "password": "secret",
            },
        ),
    },
});
    @endcode

    @section sshauthbanner Pre-Authentication Banners

    Set @ref Qore::Ssh::SshListenerConfig "SshListenerConfig.auth_banner" to
    display a message to the client before the first authentication exchange.
    The banner is sent automatically by @c authenticateSession() when
    configured.

    @code{.py}
hash<SshListenerConfig> listener = <SshListenerConfig>{
    "name": "main",
    "bind_address": "0.0.0.0",
    "port": 2222,
    "host_keys": ("/etc/ssh/host_key",),
    "auth_banner": "Authorized access only.\n",
};
    @endcode

    @section sshauthcustom Custom Auth Providers

    For full control, subclass
    @ref SshServerAuthProvider::AbstractSshAuthProvider "AbstractSshAuthProvider"
    and implement the @c authenticate() method.  The method receives a
    @ref Qore::Ssh::SshAuthContextInfo "SshAuthContextInfo" hash and must
    return a @ref Qore::Ssh::SshAuthDecision "SshAuthDecision".

    @code{.py}
class MyAuthProvider inherits AbstractSshAuthProvider {
    hash<SshAuthDecision> authenticate(hash<SshAuthContextInfo> ctx) {
        bool ok = check_credentials(ctx.username, ctx.password);
        return <SshAuthDecision>{
            "accepted": ok,
            "principal": ok ? ctx.username : NOTHING,
            "message": ok ? "welcome" : "access denied",
        };
    }
}
    @endcode

    Attach the provider to the server through
    @ref Qore::Ssh::SshServerConfig "SshServerConfig.auth_provider".

    @section sshauthlogging Authentication Logging

    When a @c LoggerInterface is attached (via
    @ref SshServerAuthProvider::VirtualSshAuthProviderOptions "VirtualSshAuthProviderOptions.logger"
    or @ref Qore::Ssh::SshServerConfig "SshServerConfig.logger"), the
    provider emits messages at three levels:

    | Level    | What is logged                                          |
    |----------|---------------------------------------------------------|
    | @c detail| Every auth attempt: method name and username             |
    | @c info  | Accepted authentications: method, username, principal, partial flag |
    | @c warn  | Rejected authentications: method, username, rejection reason |

    The server-level @c authenticateSession() method additionally logs
    public-key probe acceptances and final accept/reject outcomes at the
    @c info level.
*/
